file session-logs/README.md 20260907 opened; 20260906 closed at 132 rows counted on disk rather than carried from the parked draft
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- two want your word and one is procedural. THE OPEN: must a lap's cold roster pass FINISH before the lap may begin? Holding still while it runs is written; reading its verdict before starting is not, and the gap cost this lap 576 duplicated lines while the answer sat in the box. A loop could enforce it in one line. THE SHAPE: the star graph walks shortest at 4.79, is the most fragile shape in the paper, and carries 10.6x the better torus's non-local repair -- retire it from the candidate set, or does the mean still buy its way in? AND THE NEXT PAPER IS SIZED: my discarded instrument found, at 30 percent occupancy of a 720-address sky, that a lowest-free allocator keeps a torus perfectly routable with the stale table where random assignment shatters it into components -- and that the same policy destroys the star graph, because contiguous means something in a coordinate space and nothing in a permutation space. No witness binds that yet, so it is named as a question rather than claimed. It is the growth regime, and it is the one a network actually starts in.
